aerographene: terminal — t: colado/solto não roda sozinho; canal preso à navegação (v0.3, correção do review da C6).

Origem: aerographene (original). Licença: GPL-3.0.
Depende de: aerographene/terminal-c6.patch e aerographene/terminal-c6-page.patch.
Propósito: (1) o comando de "t: <comando>" só é enviado com Enter quando o
texto foi digitado na command bar. aerographene::TypedInputTracker
(aero_terminal_command.h), alimentado pelo OmniboxEditModel, marca como não
digitado o que veio por colagem (PasteState), inserção de vários caracteres
numa edição (clique do meio, IME), SetUserText (arrastar e soltar,
restauração, ações); "colar e acessar" chega com pasted_text. OpenMatch marca
o match (additional_info "aero_terminal_typed"); ChromeOmniboxClient passa
run ao canal; a página manda "\r" só com run === true. (2) O comando pendente
fica preso ao id da navegação que abre chrome://terminal/?new=1
(terminal_launch_watcher: WebContentsObserver) e cai se ela falhar, for
cancelada ou a aba navegar para outro lugar; só é entregue depois que ela
confirmou, e TerminalHandler::HandleStart só o pega com a página em ?new=1.
Testes: AeroTerminalCommandTest.*, TerminalLaunchTest.*.

--- a/components/omnibox/browser/aero_terminal_command.h
+++ b/components/omnibox/browser/aero_terminal_command.h
@@ -26,6 +26,39 @@
 // with or without a command.
 std::string TerminalCommandUrl();
 
+// Fatia C6b: "t: <command>" only runs by itself (Enter included) when the
+// command bar text was typed key by key. Text that arrived by paste (Ctrl+V,
+// menu, middle click), drag and drop, paste-and-go, or was set by the
+// browser (SetUserText, tab switch) is only written at the prompt and the
+// user confirms with Enter. OmniboxEditModel feeds this tracker; it errs on
+// the side of "not typed" (an IME commit of several characters counts as not
+// typed, which only costs one extra Enter).
+class TypedInputTracker {
+ public:
+  // An edit of the command bar text. `pasted`: the edit was a paste the
+  // model knows about. More than one unit added in one edit is also treated
+  // as an insertion that was not typed. Emptying the text starts over.
+  void OnTextChanged(std::u16string_view old_text,
+                     std::u16string_view new_text,
+                     bool pasted);
+  // Text set at once (drop, restore, actions): not typed unless empty.
+  void OnTextSet(std::u16string_view text);
+  // Command bar reverted to the page URL.
+  void Reset();
+  bool typed() const { return !untyped_; }
+
+ private:
+  bool untyped_ = false;
+};
+
+// AutocompleteMatch::additional_info key OmniboxEditModel::OpenMatch sets to
+// "1" when the text was typed and not paste-and-go; ChromeOmniboxClient only
+// lets the command run by itself when it finds it.
+inline constexpr char kTerminalTypedInfoKey[] = "aero_terminal_typed";
+bool TerminalInputWasTyped(std::u16string_view pasted_text,
+                           bool model_says_pasted,
+                           const TypedInputTracker& tracker);
+
 }  // namespace aerographene
 
 #endif  // COMPONENTS_OMNIBOX_BROWSER_AERO_TERMINAL_COMMAND_H_
--- a/components/omnibox/browser/aero_terminal_command.cc
+++ b/components/omnibox/browser/aero_terminal_command.cc
@@ -31,4 +31,28 @@
   return "chrome://terminal/?new=1";
 }
 
+void TypedInputTracker::OnTextChanged(std::u16string_view old_text,
+                                      std::u16string_view new_text,
+                                      bool pasted) {
+  if (new_text.empty()) {
+    untyped_ = false;
+  } else if (pasted || new_text.size() > old_text.size() + 1) {
+    untyped_ = true;
+  }
+}
+
+void TypedInputTracker::OnTextSet(std::u16string_view text) {
+  untyped_ = !text.empty();
+}
+
+void TypedInputTracker::Reset() {
+  untyped_ = false;
+}
+
+bool TerminalInputWasTyped(std::u16string_view pasted_text,
+                           bool model_says_pasted,
+                           const TypedInputTracker& tracker) {
+  return pasted_text.empty() && !model_says_pasted && tracker.typed();
+}
+
 }  // namespace aerographene
